      "comprehension_passage": "Consider a CBOW model for learning word embeddings. The vocabulary is made up of three words, {good, bad, ugly}. W and C are the matrices that contain the word and context embeddings respectively. The columns in each matrix correspond to the embeddings. Both matrices are of shape 2 x 3: [IMAGE: /data/images/cs3004_2025T2_ET_AN_p8_Im1.webp|block] The context window is 1, meaning, the next word is predicted using just the current word as context. Recall that we use softmax to make predictions at the output.",
